\section{The sandwich variance}{

\itemize{
\item \code{deli_bread_na}, a warning: the bread matrix holds \code{NA}, so no inverse of
it exists. A fit records no variance and carries on; \code{\link[=compute_sandwich]{compute_sandwich()}}
has nothing but a matrix to return and converts it into the error below.
\item \code{deli_bread_not_invertible}: the bread cannot be inverted and
\code{allow_pinv = FALSE} refused the pseudo-inverse, or it is rectangular and
has no inverse at any rank, or it holds \code{NA}.
}
}

\section{Differentiation}{

\itemize{
\item \code{deli_exact_unsupported_function}: under \code{deriv_method = "exact"}, a
function reached with a tangent-carrying argument has no rule, either
because it hands its argument to compiled code without dispatching or
because deli declines to differentiate it. \code{\link[=auto_differentiation]{auto_differentiation()}} names
the replacements to use instead.
\item \code{deli_exact_unsupported_shape}: the tangents survived but arrived in a
container the summing step has no rule for. Nothing was lost; the shape is
the problem.
\item \code{deli_exact_tangent_lost}: derivative information is gone or would be,
either because a tangent-carrying value was asked to become a plain double
or because a result arrived with no tangent and evidence that one had been
dropped on the way.
\item \code{deli_finite_difference_lost}, a warning: a finite-difference step changed
the function by less than the floating-point spacing of its values, so an
entry of the Jacobian carries none of the digits of the values it came
from.
}
}

\section{Parameter names}{

\itemize{
\item \code{deli_param_name_collision}: filling the unnamed entries of a partly named
parameter vector with positional \code{theta_1}, \code{theta_2}, ... labels would
repeat a label another parameter in the same vector already carries.
}
